(1. Project Overview) Tj
T*
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(SYNTHETIC SAMPLE DOCUMENT created for the ResearchPilot demo. Lakeside Technical) Tj
T*
(University, its people, and all figures in this report are fictional.) Tj
T*
(The Lakeside Technical University Campus Microgrid Pilot ran from March 2024 to February) Tj
T*
(2025 on the university's north campus. The pilot connected three buildings, the) Tj
T*
(Engineering Hall, the Library Annex, and the Student Services Center, to a shared solar) Tj
T*
(and battery system that can operate either connected to the regional grid or in island) Tj
T*
(mode during outages.) Tj
T*
(The project had three goals: reduce electricity costs for the connected buildings, keep) Tj
T*
(critical services running during grid outages, and give engineering students a working) Tj
T*
(energy system to study.) Tj
T*
(The solar array has a peak capacity of 1.2 megawatts and is installed on the rooftops of) Tj
T*
(the three buildings and on a covered parking structure next to the Library Annex. The) Tj
T*
(pilot was led by the university Facilities Office with support from the Department of) Tj
T*
(Electrical Engineering.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
