(2. Battery Storage Design) Tj
T*
T*
/F1 11 Tf
(The microgrid uses a lithium iron phosphate \(LFP\) battery system with a usable capacity) Tj
T*
(of 2.4 megawatt-hours, housed in two outdoor containers beside the Student Services) Tj
T*
(Center.) Tj
T*
(The project team selected LFP chemistry over nickel manganese cobalt \(NMC\) for two main) Tj
T*
(reasons. First, LFP cells have a lower risk of thermal runaway, which mattered because) Tj
T*
(the containers sit close to occupied buildings. Second, LFP cells offered a longer) Tj
T*
(expected cycle life, rated at about 6,000 full cycles, which suits a system that charges) Tj
T*
(and discharges every day.) Tj
T*
(The trade-off is lower energy density: the LFP system needed roughly 20 percent more) Tj
T*
(floor space than a comparable NMC system would have required. The team judged the extra) Tj
T*
(space acceptable because land next to the containers was available.) Tj
T*
(The battery management system limits daily depth of discharge to 85 percent to extend) Tj
T*
(battery life.) Tj
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
